What the pre-rewrite row of the corpus changes before it analyses anything.

Monarch at commit e787664, the last one before the rewrite, does not compile.
These are the three repairs that get it through solc, and they are here as a
diff so the row's count can be checked against exactly what was analysed. None
of them is in a validation path, and `validatePaymasterUserOp` and everything
it calls are untouched.

  - IModule.sol declares `ModulePaused` as an event and again as an error.
    The error is never used, so it goes.
  - BasePayments.sol writes a getter by hand with the same name as its own
    public immutable. The immutable's generated getter replaces it.
  - Security.sol leaves the visibility and the opening brace off
    `requireOwner`.

Applied by run-corpus.sh with `git apply`, which skips this preamble.

diff --git a/contracts/interfaces/IModule.sol b/contracts/interfaces/IModule.sol
--- a/contracts/interfaces/IModule.sol
+++ b/contracts/interfaces/IModule.sol
@@ -18,3 +18,2 @@ interface IModule {
     error ModuleAlreadyInitialized();
-    error ModulePaused();
     error InvalidConfiguration(string reason);
